From 4af8ae0c82ab941e1dc1c2053c10a94bc63f01cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DoubleGate <parobek@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 05:34:54 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [UPSTREAM] check: recording-level permanent-identity-exposure
 summary (T-OR-060)

rayhunter-check now tallies, per recording, how often the network obtained or
targeted a UE's permanent identity (IMSI/IMEI): events from the identity
disclosure, IMSI-requested and IMSI-paging analyzers, grouped by analyzer. The
count appears in the summary log and as an `identity_exposure` map in the JSON
report, so an operator can gauge a recording's exposure without grepping every
event.

A `0` entry is seeded for each identity-exposure analyzer that is ENABLED in the
run, so an enabled-but-clean recording (explicit 0) is distinguishable from one
where those analyzers were never active (the key absent). The tally counts an
event from a listed analyzer at any severity (they emit warning-level events,
but the count is not gated on severity like `warnings`).

This is a report-side aggregate over events the harness already produces -- no
analyzer-trait or analysis change. Also moves the check test module to the end
of the file so the crate is clippy-clean (items-after-test-module).

Tests: the tally counts only the identity-exposure analyzers; a guard test
asserts every IDENTITY_EXPOSURE_ANALYZERS name matches a real Analyzer::get_name
in a harness with those analyzers enabled (so a rename cannot silently zero the
count); seeding and an Informational-severity case are covered.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
